### Description

The documentation for [`RegionInfo(int culture)`](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.globalization.regioninfo.-ctor?view=net-6.0#system-globalization-regioninfo-ctor(system-int32)) says it will throw an `ArgumentException` when "`culture` specifies either an invariant, custom, or neutral culture."

However, when passed a value of 4096 (LOCALE_CUSTOM_UNSPECIFIED) the constructor behaves differently depending on preceding method calls.

### Reproduction Steps

```cs
using System;
using System.Globalization;
using System.Linq;

if (args.Contains("get-cultures"))
{
    CultureInfo.GetCultures(CultureTypes.SpecificCultures);
}

if (args.Contains("ai"))
{
    new RegionInfo("ai");
}

Console.WriteLine(new RegionInfo(4096).EnglishName);
```

### Expected behavior

I expect `new RegionInfo(4096)` to throw an `ArgumentException`, regardless of the preceding method calls.

### Actual behavior

On my machine:

If run without arguments, the program prints "Australia".

If run with the argument "get-cultures", the program prints "Ethiopia".

If run with the argument "ai", the program throws an `ArgumentException` with the message "Culture ID 4096 (0x1000) is a neutral culture; a region cannot be created from it. (Parameter 'culture')".


